</code>
The index of x in the new array list should be equal to the last index of x in the old array list plus one. This assert statement checks if the new item was inserted at the correct position, after the last occurrence of x in the old list.

<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == old_arrListContainsX);
</code>
The new array list should still contain the old value of x, as neither the count of x nor its index in the list is expected to be changed by the insert operation. The contains operation will return the correct result even if an element was inserted.

<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);
</code>
The count of the new array list should be one more than the old count. This will confirm that an element was inserted at the designated position.

<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX);
</code>
The last index of x in the new list should be the same as the index of x in the new list. This aligns with the requirement that the insert operation should not disturb the ordering of x in the list.

